    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1701">

                <pb facs="1446" n="1342" sameAs="frus:frus1913/pg1342"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 367.11/146.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The American Ambassador to the Secretary of State.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 481.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Embassy</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Constantinople</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1913-04-29">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">April 29, 1913</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to the Embassy’s despatch No.
                    429 of February 24, 1913, on the subject of requisitions for war purposes, I
                    have the honor to enclose herewith a copy and translation of the Porte’s reply
                    [Enclosure 4] to the note verbale identique therein transmitted; also copies and
                    translations of notes exchanged between the diplomatic missions and the Porte in
                    regard to the occupation of foreigners’ houses at San Stefano by Ottoman
                    troops.</p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">W. W. Rockhill</hi>.</signed>
                </closer>







